1
00:00:00,552 --> 00:00:02,722
Tesla just built a flying car.

2
00:00:03,080 --> 00:00:05,026
That's the headline. It's also

3
00:00:05,352 --> 00:00:06,402
Not quite true.

4
00:00:07,112 --> 00:00:08,418
and the part that isn't true

5
00:00:08,776 --> 00:00:10,242
That's the entire story.

6
00:00:10,920 --> 00:00:18,562
Give me 11 minutes. I'll show you exactly how this thing leaves the ground with no wings, no rotors, no propellers, nothing.

7
00:00:19,528 --> 00:00:23,714
I'll show you the one engineering detail Tesla hopes you never think about.

8
00:00:24,104 --> 00:00:27,522
because it decides whether this car ever actually flies.

9
00:00:28,104 --> 00:00:30,818
And at the end, I'll tell you what it really is.

10
00:00:31,304 --> 00:00:32,962
because it's not a flying car.

11
00:00:33,864 --> 00:00:37,410
Everything you're about to hear comes from the actual event footage.

12
00:00:37,832 --> 00:00:40,194
Tesla's own posts and the physics.

13
00:00:40,552 --> 00:00:41,762
not the press release.

14
00:00:42,088 --> 00:00:42,690
Let's go

15
00:00:43,560 --> 00:00:45,954
October 15, 2026.

16
00:00:46,344 --> 00:00:47,618
Not a car showroom.

17
00:00:48,072 --> 00:00:49,378
Not an auto expo.

18
00:00:50,536 --> 00:01:00,994
SpaceX's rocket test facility in McGregor, Texas, 7.55 in the evening, fog on the ground, red lasers in the air, and a ramp that looks like a half pipe.

19
00:01:01,832 --> 00:01:03,202
The car rolls up that ramp.

20
00:01:03,528 --> 00:01:04,834
with nobody inside it.

21
00:01:05,352 --> 00:01:06,882
climbs to full inversion.

22
00:01:07,240 --> 00:01:08,066
Upside down.

23
00:01:08,712 --> 00:01:10,722
Then it launches into a barrel roll.

24
00:01:11,112 --> 00:01:14,626
does a kickflip over five Teslas lined up on the tarmac?

25
00:01:15,016 --> 00:01:18,882
including a semi, and then a corkscrew straight off the ground.

26
00:01:19,400 --> 00:01:22,722
0 to 60 in 0.81 seconds.

27
00:01:23,112 --> 00:01:24,322
That's Tesla's number.

28
00:01:24,712 --> 00:01:26,882
Hold onto it. We're coming back to it.

29
00:01:27,560 --> 00:01:30,114
Musk walks out and says three words.

30
00:01:30,472 --> 00:01:31,970
Flying cars are real.

31
00:01:32,392 --> 00:01:34,434
Then, almost under his breath.

32
00:01:34,760 --> 00:01:36,162
Well, it worked.

33
00:01:36,520 --> 00:01:45,250
Here's the thing, nobody in the crowd seemed to notice. The car was driverless. Musk's own explanation to make sure we don't kill anyone.

34
00:01:45,800 --> 00:01:46,690
That's a joke.

35
00:01:47,016 --> 00:01:48,322
It's also a confession.

36
00:01:48,904 --> 00:01:50,306
and ask yourself this.

37
00:01:50,696 --> 00:02:00,962
Why does a car launch need a rocket range? Why did the original October 1 date get postponed for high winds, with FAA airspace closures over the site?

38
00:02:01,384 --> 00:02:03,458
A road car doesn't care about wind.

39
00:02:04,104 --> 00:02:06,050
car that leaves the ground does.

40
00:02:06,440 --> 00:02:09,058
That postponement told you what the event wouldn't.

41
00:02:09,384 --> 00:02:13,090
This thing flies like an aircraft with aircraft problems.

42
00:02:13,544 --> 00:02:16,418
No wings, no rotors, no propellers.

43
00:02:16,808 --> 00:02:17,442
So how?

44
00:02:18,184 --> 00:02:21,026
systems and they do opposite jobs.

45
00:02:21,640 --> 00:02:23,714
First, cold gas thrusters.

46
00:02:24,328 --> 00:02:37,666
10 nozzles mounted around the car, fed by 600 liters of compressed air stored in rocket-grade carbon tanks. COPVs, the exact same tank technology SpaceX bolts onto its rockets.

47
00:02:38,024 --> 00:02:42,146
Tesla's words, "Every usable void in the car is packed with them."

48
00:02:42,568 --> 00:02:43,522
No combustion.

49
00:02:43,880 --> 00:02:45,634
No flame, no fuel.

50
00:02:46,216 --> 00:02:49,506
Just ultra high pressure air fired through nozzles.

51
00:02:49,928 --> 00:02:53,154
the same principle as a spacecraft's attitude thrusters.

52
00:02:53,544 --> 00:02:56,226
Musk claims 80 kN of thrust.

53
00:02:56,648 --> 00:02:59,586
That's his number, not an independent measurement.

54
00:03:00,168 --> 00:03:00,610
2nd

55
00:03:01,032 --> 00:03:06,114
a giant suction fan under the floor that literally sucks the car onto the road.

56
00:03:06,632 --> 00:03:09,154
Tesla claims more than two Gs of grip.

57
00:03:09,512 --> 00:03:12,802
"Enough," they say, to drive the thing upside down.

58
00:03:13,448 --> 00:03:14,946
so the thrusters push it up.

59
00:03:15,272 --> 00:03:16,930
The fan pushes it down.

60
00:03:17,512 --> 00:03:19,682
two systems opposite directions.

61
00:03:20,136 --> 00:03:22,882
Now here's my take, and I want you to sit with this.

62
00:03:23,304 --> 00:03:24,930
The thrusters are the marketing.

63
00:03:25,416 --> 00:03:27,202
The Suction fan is the product.

64
00:03:27,720 --> 00:03:28,162
Why?

65
00:03:28,552 --> 00:03:31,330
because the thrusters run on a finite tank of air.

66
00:03:31,752 --> 00:03:35,010
and Tesla's own X account said the quiet part out loud.

67
00:03:35,400 --> 00:03:38,658
More compressed gas on board equals more flight time.

68
00:03:39,080 --> 00:03:42,594
Read that again? That's Tesla telling you the tank is the limit.

69
00:03:43,464 --> 00:03:48,674
But this story didn't start last week. It started nine years ago with People's Money.

70
00:03:49,320 --> 00:03:50,306
2017.

71
00:03:50,632 --> 00:03:59,202
Musk reveals the Roadster, 0-60 in 1.9 seconds, 620 miles of range, $200,000.

72
00:03:59,624 --> 00:04:03,554
Thousands of people wire $50,000 deposits that night.

73
00:04:03,944 --> 00:04:06,018
Production promised for 2020.

74
00:04:06,440 --> 00:04:07,682
What did those people get?

75
00:04:08,008 --> 00:04:08,866
Hold that thought.

76
00:04:09,256 --> 00:04:12,514
2018, Musk tweets the SpaceX package.

77
00:04:12,840 --> 00:04:14,850
10 rocket thrusters around the car.

78
00:04:15,816 --> 00:04:20,162
2019, someone posts an animation of a flying DeLorean.

79
00:04:20,616 --> 00:04:21,634
Musk replies.

80
00:04:21,960 --> 00:04:24,738
the roadster will actually do something like this.

81
00:04:25,192 --> 00:04:26,658
Then silence.

82
00:04:27,112 --> 00:04:31,362
2020 comes and goes. 2021, 2022.

83
00:04:31,720 --> 00:04:34,338
2023, every date slips.

84
00:04:35,176 --> 00:04:44,098
Musk says the design goals have been radically increased.

85
00:04:44,424 --> 00:04:45,090
doesn't happen.

86
00:04:45,576 --> 00:04:51,618
November 2025. He finally sets a demo date. April 1st, 2026.

87
00:04:52,104 --> 00:04:57,154
And he jokes that the date gives him deniability, because I can say I was just kidding.

88
00:04:57,800 --> 00:05:01,026
April 1 passes, then hopefully next month.

89
00:05:01,384 --> 00:05:02,274
than August.

90
00:05:02,600 --> 00:05:03,106
Nothing.

91
00:05:03,784 --> 00:05:08,898
September 12th, go for launch. October 1st, postponed. Wind.

92
00:05:09,384 --> 00:05:12,002
October 15th, it finally happens.

93
00:05:12,744 --> 00:05:18,466
9 years, 8 slipped dates, 1 car that left the ground for a few seconds,

94
00:05:18,920 --> 00:05:20,610
Here's what actually got announced.

95
00:05:21,000 --> 00:05:22,018
3 trims.

96
00:05:22,472 --> 00:05:27,842
Performance, two seats, under 1.6 seconds, suction system only.

97
00:05:28,264 --> 00:05:29,826
Tesla calls it "road ready."

98
00:05:30,696 --> 00:05:36,002
Thrust 2 seats under 0.9 seconds. Rear thrusters added.

99
00:05:36,360 --> 00:05:37,058
Race Ready!

100
00:05:37,576 --> 00:05:38,082
Rocket

101
00:05:38,408 --> 00:05:44,258
One seat under 0.59 seconds. 10 perimeter thrusters. Air ready.

102
00:05:44,744 --> 00:05:45,890
Notice what just happened.

103
00:05:46,312 --> 00:05:49,474
Only the top trim flies. It has one seat.

104
00:05:50,216 --> 00:05:51,586
and its invite only.

105
00:05:52,296 --> 00:05:53,730
So when the headlines say,

106
00:05:54,088 --> 00:05:55,554
Tesla's Flying Car

107
00:05:56,104 --> 00:05:59,298
They're talking about a machine almost nobody can buy.

108
00:05:59,976 --> 00:06:02,306
and those 2017 deposit holders,

109
00:06:02,856 --> 00:06:04,258
Reservations reopen.

110
00:06:05,000 --> 00:06:07,042
$50,000 for performance.

111
00:06:07,400 --> 00:06:09,410
250,000 for thrust.

112
00:06:10,184 --> 00:06:11,458
The one that flies?

113
00:06:11,848 --> 00:06:12,802
You don't apply.

114
00:06:13,160 --> 00:06:14,146
You get invited.

115
00:06:14,792 --> 00:06:16,226
9 years of waiting

116
00:06:16,584 --> 00:06:19,138
and the car that leaves the ground isn't for sale.

117
00:06:19,912 --> 00:06:23,042
Let's talk about 0.81 seconds.

118
00:06:23,720 --> 00:06:26,786
Tesla demoed it on stage, and I want to be fair.

119
00:06:27,528 --> 00:06:30,018
I believe the car is absurdly fast.

120
00:06:30,824 --> 00:06:36,002
But that number is the least honest number of the whole night. And not because it's fake.

121
00:06:36,424 --> 00:06:41,794
It was measured by Tesla on a closed rocket range in a car with no driver.

122
00:06:42,152 --> 00:06:44,962
with no independent instrument anywhere in sight.

123
00:06:45,544 --> 00:06:56,706
Not one figure from that night, not the 0.81, not the 80 kN, not the 250 kilos of air, has been verified by anyone outside Tesla.

124
00:06:57,160 --> 00:06:58,434
Now compare honestly.

125
00:06:58,792 --> 00:07:02,082
The Rimac Nevera does 1.74 seconds.

126
00:07:02,408 --> 00:07:03,874
independently verified.

127
00:07:04,200 --> 00:07:07,042
Road Legal – $2.2 million.

128
00:07:07,720 --> 00:07:12,706
Pininfarina Battista 1.79 Verified at Nardò

129
00:07:13,384 --> 00:07:20,162
If the rocket trim's Sub-0.59 claim holds, it beats everything ever made by a full second.

130
00:07:20,552 --> 00:07:23,266
"If" is doing a lot of work in that sentence.

131
00:07:23,944 --> 00:07:27,458
Claimed versus verified. Never compare them as equals.

132
00:07:27,976 --> 00:07:28,770
That's the rule

133
00:07:29,384 --> 00:07:30,242
and honestly

134
00:07:30,696 --> 00:07:33,314
Tesla's best framing came from their own account.

135
00:07:33,768 --> 00:07:38,210
The thruster system generates four to five times the force the tires can handle.

136
00:07:38,792 --> 00:07:40,098
That's the honest pitch.

137
00:07:40,488 --> 00:07:42,754
This is about acceleration not flight.

138
00:07:43,176 --> 00:07:44,642
The flying is the marketing.

139
00:07:45,096 --> 00:07:46,530
The launch is the product.

140
00:07:47,048 --> 00:07:52,130
The most savage response to the reveal didn't come from a critic. It came from a rival.

141
00:07:52,552 --> 00:07:58,882
Alef Aeronautics, a company that spent 11 years building an actual road-driveable flying car.

142
00:07:59,240 --> 00:08:03,394
FAA-certified. Already hand-building customer cars.

143
00:08:03,752 --> 00:08:06,818
hosted a video of their car flying over the new Roadster.

144
00:08:07,272 --> 00:08:15,906
Their CEO, Jim Dukhovny, with a straight face, welcome Tesla, to the flying car race. We've been here alone for 11 years.

145
00:08:16,552 --> 00:08:20,098
That is the entire industry dynamic in one sentence.

146
00:08:20,520 --> 00:08:21,986
and he's not alone out there.

147
00:08:22,312 --> 00:08:27,938
XPeng is shipping a flying car carrier with 7,000 pre-orders, deliveries this year.

148
00:08:28,488 --> 00:08:33,666
Joby is putting actual passengers in electric aircraft before the year ends.

149
00:08:34,056 --> 00:08:34,754
and Lilium.

150
00:08:35,176 --> 00:08:37,314
raised a billion and a half dollars.

151
00:08:37,672 --> 00:08:40,546
peaked at a 3.3 billion valuation.

152
00:08:40,904 --> 00:08:41,602
is dead.

153
00:08:42,024 --> 00:08:44,738
never delivered a single commercial aircraft.

154
00:08:45,256 --> 00:08:47,618
Here's the positioning nobody says out loud.

155
00:08:48,072 --> 00:08:50,082
Alef and XPeng sell travel.

156
00:08:50,760 --> 00:08:52,386
Joby sells rides.

157
00:08:52,744 --> 00:08:54,338
Tesla sells spectacle.

158
00:08:54,760 --> 00:08:58,850
The Roadster is the only flying car here that can't go anywhere.

159
00:08:59,240 --> 00:09:01,442
that's the Honest Differentiator.

160
00:09:01,896 --> 00:09:02,402
Now?

161
00:09:02,920 --> 00:09:05,378
detail Tesla hopes you don't think about.

162
00:09:05,832 --> 00:09:07,906
250 kilograms of air.

163
00:09:08,264 --> 00:09:09,378
That's the whole tank.

164
00:09:09,992 --> 00:09:10,658
All of it.

165
00:09:11,176 --> 00:09:16,770
The only public estimate of burn rate, around 27 kilos a second at full thrust.

166
00:09:17,160 --> 00:09:20,642
Do the math and you get single digit seconds of full thrust.

167
00:09:21,000 --> 00:09:22,850
seconds, not minutes.

168
00:09:23,304 --> 00:09:25,698
Tesla has never published a flight duration.

169
00:09:26,088 --> 00:09:27,202
Now you know why.

170
00:09:27,848 --> 00:09:28,642
It hops.

171
00:09:29,224 --> 00:09:31,490
It flips. It does not travel.

172
00:09:32,072 --> 00:09:41,890
Then the refill question, which nobody asked on stage. The car refills its own tanks, but Tesla won't say how fast. How many hops per hour?

173
00:09:42,216 --> 00:09:42,786
Unknown.

174
00:09:43,304 --> 00:09:48,162
and the questions Musk dodged, someone in the crowd shouted about street legality.

175
00:09:48,648 --> 00:09:50,562
His entire answer. Yeah.

176
00:09:50,952 --> 00:09:52,162
depends on your street.

177
00:09:52,648 --> 00:09:53,314
That's it.

178
00:09:53,736 --> 00:09:55,010
That's the whole answer.

179
00:09:55,432 --> 00:09:57,090
No final price announced.

180
00:09:57,448 --> 00:10:02,594
No FAA certificate in federal records. One was checked for. None found.

181
00:10:02,952 --> 00:10:07,170
Tesla's own website says the car is not approved for public road use.

182
00:10:07,752 --> 00:10:24,066
And the noise, the thrusters were deafening on the live stream, fired for only a few seconds near the audience. Now imagine 10 rocket nozzles going off in traffic. No regulator on earth is approving that. A car that can fly, but may never be allowed to.

183
00:10:24,456 --> 00:10:24,930
So

184
00:10:25,448 --> 00:10:26,850
What is it? Really.

185
00:10:27,560 --> 00:10:28,802
Here's my honest take.

186
00:10:29,256 --> 00:10:35,938
This is a sub-second, suction-gripped, thruster-assisted track monster wearing a flying car costume.

187
00:10:36,520 --> 00:10:37,698
and the costume worked.

188
00:10:38,088 --> 00:10:39,650
Because we're all talking about it.

189
00:10:40,296 --> 00:10:44,034
Musk called it "the best of the last human-driven cars."

190
00:10:44,776 --> 00:10:49,026
He admitted the revenue impact is a "small potato situation."

191
00:10:49,352 --> 00:10:53,186
He teased, jumping Evel Knievel's Snake River Canyon jump.

192
00:10:53,832 --> 00:10:55,138
Read between those lines.

193
00:10:55,624 --> 00:10:57,634
Even he knows this isn't a business.

194
00:10:58,088 --> 00:10:58,850
It's a h

195
00:10:59,304 --> 00:11:00,034
A statement.

196
00:11:00,488 --> 00:11:02,914
the world's most spectacular science project.

197
00:11:03,976 --> 00:11:11,330
But here's the twist. Nobody's saying the same thrusters that make it fly make it impossible to sell as a road car.

198
00:11:11,688 --> 00:11:15,170
the noise, the back blast, the certification wall.

199
00:11:15,560 --> 00:11:20,322
The physics that makes the demo possible is exactly what keeps it off your street.

200
00:11:20,840 --> 00:11:22,754
Tesla didn't build a flying car.

201
00:11:23,720 --> 00:11:25,474
They built a rocket you can park.

202
00:11:26,120 --> 00:11:26,850
And honestly?

203
00:11:27,240 --> 00:11:28,738
That's way more interesting.

204
00:11:29,352 --> 00:11:30,562
If you want the next one,

205
00:11:30,920 --> 00:11:36,642
the full breakdown of what it would actually take to make this thing street legal, and why nobody's close.

206
00:11:37,032 --> 00:11:38,882
That's the video I'm making next.

207
00:11:39,272 --> 00:11:40,064
See you there.
